# 14. Planned Pi Storage

The user has chosen an NVMe-based Pi installation.

Hardware plan:

```text
Raspberry Pi 5
    |
Official Raspberry Pi M.2 HAT+
    |
2242 NVMe SSD
```

The HAT is the genuine Raspberry Pi M.2 HAT+ selected from CanaKit.

The intention is to boot/use the Pi from NVMe and keep the application and SQLite database on the NVMe rather than relying on microSD for the long-term installation.

A 2242 NVMe is required for the selected HAT configuration. Do not substitute a 2280 drive without a compatible HAT/adapter.

